# Meridian Front: a sci-fi real-time strategy campaign invented as a genre example. No game's
# names, data or logic. An expedition fights its way across four planets, one chapter each.
# Missions open from a war room in a tree; each mission has three objectives, and each
# objective is a check. Items are planet coordinates (they open a chapter), unit types and
# upgrades.
world meridian_front "Meridian Front" version 1
use army
use campaign
use finales
use war_room
start war_room

# How long the campaign is: the chapters past this one are left out, missions and all.
option chapters: range 2..4 = 4
# Side operations are optional missions off the main line.
option side_ops: toggle = on
# `tree` keeps the mission tree; `open` lets any mission of a planet you can reach be
# played in any order.
option campaign_order: choice(tree, open) = tree

# The first planet's coordinates and the rifle squads are there from the start.
start_item halvar_coordinates
start_item rifle_squad

# The campaign is won when the finale of each chapter in play is won.
goal counter(chapter_won) >= opt.chapters
